Phase 25 - make page-inflight-check: the evidence that it can fail
==================================================================

A gate that has only ever been seen GREEN is indistinguishable from a gate that
cannot fail, so every verdict below was measured rather than reasoned about, and
the exit status is recorded next to it. The tree was committed before every
break, and restored and checked clean after it.

WHERE THIS WAS TAKEN, because it is not the usual place. The chat session that
wrote this phase ran the gate in its own sandbox, against its own clone, with
CHROMIUM_PATH pointing at chromium-1194 rather than the build Playwright 1.62
pins. That is a different machine and a different browser from the devbox, and
`one definition, two hosts` is a trap this project has already paid for. So this
log is evidence that the gate CAN fail and that each break reddens the claim it
is aimed at - it is not evidence about the devbox. Re-running it there is a
one-line job and the numbers should be identical; if they are not, that
difference is the finding.

The first entry is not a break test. It is the gate run against the page AS IT
STOOD, before anything was fixed - which is stronger evidence than a
re-introduced defect, because the defect was already there and 20m had watched a
live cycle print it.

